WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:15.748
Gunnar took Vinnie to the back of the blacksmith's shop.

2
00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:21.287
He wanted Vinnie to see the Viking swords.

3
00:00:21.288 --> 00:00:26.878
Mandy watched Old Dirk, the blacksmith, open the jewelry box.

4
00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:31.877
It was filled with bracelets, rings, and necklaces.

5
00:00:31.878 --> 00:00:36.270
"Where did those come from?" Mandy asked.

6
00:00:36.271 --> 00:00:45.336
"When people do not have anything else that is valuable," Dirk said, "Vikings take their gold."

7
00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:49.872
"You mean . . ." Mandy tried to calm herself.

8
00:00:49.873 --> 00:00:54.342
"You mean, they stole these?"

9
00:00:54.343 --> 00:00:59.615
"We Vikings take what we want," Dirk said proudly.

10
00:00:59.616 --> 00:01:04.315
"May I ask one more question?" said Mandy.

11
00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:07.346
"Sure," answered the blacksmith.

12
00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:11.603
"Why is the captain called Skull-Crusher?"

13
00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.887
Old Dirk laughed.

14
00:01:13.888 --> 00:01:22.342
"Vikings are given nicknames for their fighting skills," he explained.

15
00:01:22.343 --> 00:01:26.601
He started sorting the gold from the jewelry box.

16
00:01:26.602 --> 00:01:33.020
"What's that?" Mandy asked, spotting a small wooden bear carving.

17
00:01:33.021 --> 00:01:35.334
"It's so cute!"

18
00:01:35.335 --> 00:01:39.528
Old Dirk picked it up and looked it over.

19
00:01:39.529 --> 00:01:42.566
"Hmm. I don't know.

20
00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:45.942
It shouldn't be in here with the jewelry.

21
00:01:45.943 --> 00:01:48.334
Would you like to keep it?"

22
00:01:48.335 --> 00:01:53.080
"Yes, thank you," Mandy said with a big smile.

23
00:01:53.081 --> 00:01:57.810
She put the little bear in her pocket.

24
00:01:57.811 --> 00:02:01.664
"Gunnar, this will take a while,"

25
00:02:01.665 --> 00:02:05.411
Old Dirk called to the boys in the back.

26
00:02:05.412 --> 00:02:08.080
He started melting the gold.

27
00:02:08.081 --> 00:02:13.076
"You'll have to come back later."

28
00:02:13.077 --> 00:02:18.141
Outside the workshop, Gunnar faced Vinnie and Mandy.

29
00:02:18.142 --> 00:02:22.086
"I don't even know your names," he said.

30
00:02:22.087 --> 00:02:29.013
"Oh, sorry. I'm Vinnie and this is my sister, Mandy," said Vinnie.

31
00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:32.604
"Strange names," Gunnar remarked.

32
00:02:32.605 --> 00:02:36.085
He shrugged and began walking away.

33
00:02:36.086 --> 00:02:43.943
"So Gunnar, how long have you been with . . ."—Vinnie paused—"with Skull-Crusher?"

34
00:02:43.944 --> 00:02:47.818
"Just one year," Gunnar replied.

35
00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:51.801
"I want to be a Viking warrior like my father.

36
00:02:51.802 --> 00:02:53.911
But he was killed.

37
00:02:53.912 --> 00:02:56.283
No one would teach me to fight.

38
00:02:56.284 --> 00:02:59.607
So I hid on the Sleeping Dragon.

39
00:02:59.608 --> 00:03:03.868
The captain was upset at first, but he let me stay.

40
00:03:03.869 --> 00:03:06.404
Now I'm his aide!"

41
00:03:06.405 --> 00:03:13.091
Passing through Kaupang village, Mandy's view of the Vikings began to change.

42
00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:16.647
She saw many farmers and fishermen.

43
00:03:16.648 --> 00:03:20.078
So they weren't all robbers and warriors.

44
00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:25.337
In fact, they seemed just like most people.

45
00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:29.881
A group of children were playing a game on a field.

46
00:03:29.882 --> 00:03:32.535
A crowd gathered to watch.

47
00:03:32.536 --> 00:03:35.815
"What are they playing?" asked Vinnie.

48
00:03:35.816 --> 00:03:39.142
"Knattleikr," replied Gunnar.

49
00:03:39.143 --> 00:03:42.667
The children paused to watch for a while.

50
00:03:42.668 --> 00:03:44.942
There were two teams.

51
00:03:44.943 --> 00:03:48.082
Some players had wooden sticks.

52
00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:50.885
They were hitting a ball around.

53
00:03:50.886 --> 00:03:55.078
"It looks like hockey," remarked Mandy.

54
00:03:55.079 --> 00:03:59.546
Suddenly one player caught a flying ball.

55
00:03:59.547 --> 00:04:03.484
He threw it to another player who had a stick.

56
00:04:03.485 --> 00:04:05.989
His teammate hit the ball.

57
00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:10.691
But the ball flew wildly in the wrong direction.

58
00:04:10.692 --> 00:04:15.147
Konk! The ball hit Vinnie right on the head.

59
00:04:15.148 --> 00:04:17.906
He fell to the ground.

60
00:04:17.907 --> 00:04:20.217
His eyes were closed.

61
00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:22.476
He did not move.

62
00:04:22.477 --> 00:04:25.341
"Vinnie!" screamed Mandy.

63
00:04:25.342 --> 00:04:28.156
The crowd gathered around.

64
00:04:28.157 --> 00:04:31.334
"Is he okay?" asked someone.

65
00:04:31.335 --> 00:04:33.540
"Let's take him to my house,"

66
00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:36.406
said a boy, coming forward to help.

67
00:04:36.407 --> 00:04:39.876
Gunnar and the boy picked Vinnie up.

68
00:04:39.877 --> 00:04:47.751
Mandy followed, very worried.
